WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.801 --> 00:00:01.901
-It is January.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.000
It's freezing outside

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.234
and everyone has the blahs.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.133
That includes
my monologue writers.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.133
[ Laughter and awws ]

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.634
No, it's okay.
It's okay.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.000
They're human,
just like the rest of us.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.100
It may seem hard to believe,

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.767
but they write hundreds of jokes
every day,

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:16.634
just to get the 10 or 12 we use
in the monologue.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.400
And, let's face it,
a lot of those jokes,

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.534
you know, they're not great
and, honestly, sometimes I think

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:22.067
they just throw in
some real stinkers

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.200
to fill up the page
and meet the assignment.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:28.467
But just because it's January
and the sun goes down at 5:00 pm

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.267
doesn't mean we can
tolerate laziness,

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:33.033
which means it's time
for a "Surprise Inspection."

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.033
[ Trumpet blows reveille ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:40.100
♪♪

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.434
It's a very long intro.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:44.901
So here's how this works.

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:48.234
These are real jokes,
really submitted by my writers,

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:49.701
that are unusable for the show.

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:52.200
Some are dumb,
some are patently offensive,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.667
and some just don't make sense.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:56.100
Most importantly, the writers
don't know we're doing this

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.767
[ Audience ohs ]
and, because a lot of them
don't watch the show,

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.133
they'll never know
we're doing this.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:04.734
So let's get to it.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:07.000
The European bank Santander

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.334
took back more than $170 million

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:11.467
that they had
accidentally deposited

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:14.200
into customers' bank accounts
on Christmas Day,

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.133
due to a "scheduling issue,"

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:19.734
and it's incidents like this
that make kids stop believing

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:21.200
in Santander.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.200
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:28.934
That was written by Ian.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:34.734
And it somehow went back in time
and ruined Christmas for me.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:37.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:39.367
A Florida couple last month

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:42.000
discovered a colony
of 80,000 bees

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.701
hidden behind their shower wall.

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:44.601
Said, the wife,

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:45.534
"Honey!"

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.534
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:49.634
[ Applause ]

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.868
That was also written by Ian.

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:58.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.567
Which I think qualifies him
as a serial killer.

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:02.567
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:05.767
According to a new study,

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:08.467
playing a recording
of people's names while sleeping

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:11.701
can improve name recall
the next day.

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:12.567
"Worked for me,"

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:14.100
said Lou Bega.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.534
[ Applause ]

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:22.734
So, that one requires you
to remember

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.200
the 1999 song...

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.133
..."Mambo No. 5" and,

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:31.934
even then, not a great joke.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:34.367
I'd say that would've gone

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:36.934
maybe 2% better in 1999.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:39.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.834
Uh...

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:42.100
Wait, that was
"A little bit of...

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.367
"A little bit of Monica," right?

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:44.434
"A little bit," yeah.

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:45.934
That was okay.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:48.367
In 1999, you were allowed
to have several girlfriends.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.467
As long as only a little bit
of them were in your life.

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:54.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.133
So like Erica would say like,

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:57.434
"Are you seeing someone
named Monica?"

00:02:57.434 --> 00:02:58.400
And you were like,
"A little bit."

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.434
It was a different time,
you guys.

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:08.267
More than 800 parakeets
were recently surrendered

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.934
to a Michigan animal shelter.

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:11.200
It's been a rough month

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.701
for excessive tweeters.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:14.701
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.267
♪ A little bit of Marjorie ♪

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:23.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:27.734
A court -- 1999!

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:29.267
Most popular show -- "Friends."

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:31.100
Unlike today, where I think
it's still "Friends."

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:36.067
According to the latest numbers,
the U.S. is averaging more

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:39.634
than 386,000 new cases
of the coronavirus each day,

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:42.434
so call me Ellen DeGeneres,
because this studio audience

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.200
is all going home
with something!

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.200
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:51.400
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.667
Are you are you just clapping

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.234
because you don't know
what else to do?

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:57.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.367 --> 00:03:59.000
Is that how much you like
free things,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.033
even if it's a virus?

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:03.801
You're like, "Aah!"

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:05.267
[ Cheering ]
[ Claps ]

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.868
Rapper Cardi B tweeted yesterday
that she wanted to get

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:11.834
her son's name tattooed
on her face.

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:13.334
Fortunately, her son's name is

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:14.367
Cheek.

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:16.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.501
Karen Chee wrote that joke.

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:22.334
Karen is just an adorable,

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:24.801
adorable person.

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:25.734
There she is.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.701
[ Laughter and awws ]

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:30.667
And, yet, if you saw her now,
do remember to flip her off.

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:32.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:36.667
Let's win it.
You know what?

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:40.000
I'm going to win you guys back
with an uplifting one.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.100
Because that cheek joke was --
Let's be honest.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:46.267
We need to do a little work
to win you guys back.

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:49.367
Today was actor Mel Gibson's
66th birthday.

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:51.167
Unfortunately,
when he blew out the candles,

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:52.567
there were still some Jews.

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:54.567
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.367
So sad.

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:04.634
He had a bad birthday.

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:06.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.067
We can't do that.

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:10.734
You could never do that on TV.

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:12.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.000
Imagine what would happen if I
said that joke on television.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.868
People were at home watching TV.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:22.701
Thank God we caught it
in this "Surprise Inspection."

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:24.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:31.868
According to a new survey,
17% of Americans said

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:34.133
that they would like
to receive sexual favors

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.901
as a gift for Valentine's Day.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.133
Said the surveyor,

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:39.067
Okay, but I just did
the last house,

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:41.567
so I'm going to need like
20 minutes to get going again."

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:43.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:50.801
Former first lady Michelle Obama
turned 58 today.

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:53.534
And, by the way,
these aren't all written today.

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:55.601
I'm trying to stop
what just happened.

00:05:55.601 --> 00:05:57.734
[ Laughter ]
Not her birthday today.

00:05:57.734 --> 00:05:59.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:01.434
I would hate for you to clap
for that

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:04.367
after you clapped
about the free virus.

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:07.000
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.567
Let's take it back.
Let's get this set up

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:12.200
because this one's real nice.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.667
Let's see who wrote it.
Go before.

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:16.334
Oh, Scollins wrote this.

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:18.033
If you watch our show, you know
anything about Scollins,

00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:18.934
you know he's a bad guy.

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:21.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:24.100
Former First Lady Michelle Obama
turned 58 today

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.667
and, if you're wondering
what her secret is --

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:27.400
[ Whispering ]
Barack was born in Kenya.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.400
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:44.434
"Scream" premiered this weekend
at the box office

00:06:44.434 --> 00:06:45.934
and, if you want
to know who dies --

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:47.667
the unvaccinated audience.

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:49.667
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:57.534
This whole thing was some pri--

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:59.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:01.234
This has been
"Surprise Inspection."

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:03.300
